                <pb facs="0310" n="250" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg250"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 48.—Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Tillman to
                        General Alfaro</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1895-12-03"><hi rendition="#italic">December
                                3, 1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>By letter dated November 6, 1895, I am directed by the United States Government
                    to enter into full diplomatic relations with the ministerial officers of
                    Ecuador, of whom you are the chief. Mr. Dillard, consul-general of the United
                    States, unites with me in congratulating you and the Republic of Ecuador.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tillman</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
